     },
     "annotation_name": "K35 Circuit",
     "annotation": "Which MS-20 filter circuit the K35 model (LPF and HPF) uses. OTA (Mk2): the later LM13600 design, with clipping diodes in the resonance feedback, as in v1.5. KORG-35 (Mk1): the original Korg35 Sallen-Key, with clipping diodes in the signal path, so loud signals distort at every frequency; CHARACTER sets how hard they are driven. Reference mode runs it at 8x (LPF) / 4x (HPF). Options: OTA (Mk2), KORG-35 (Mk1). Default: OTA (Mk2).",
     "hint": "K35 Circuit: Which MS-20 filter circuit the K35 model (LPF and HPF) uses. OTA (Mk2): the later LM13600 design, with clipping diodes in the resonance feedback, as in v1.5. KORG-35 (Mk1): the original Korg35 Sallen-Key, with clipping diodes in the signal path, so loud signals distort at every frequency; CHARACTER sets how hard they are driven. Reference mode runs it at 8x (LPF) / 4x (HPF)."
    }
   },
   {
    "box": {
